  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Under One Moon",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"Under One Moon\"**\n\nAlberto de Luna's surname and his scores are moons, so the whole site lives under one. Every page is a night scene: black ink and deep petrol, moonlight paper and Alberto's blues, a royal cobalt for surfaces and a luminous sky blue for light. A score is not a number in a badge, it is the phase of a moon, and that moon recurs as the loader, the nav's progress mark, the score stamp, the footer's phase strip and the map pins. If a new screen has no moon in it somewhere, it is probably off-brand.\n\nThe voice is a late-night food column set as a poster: huge, wide, black-weight Archivo headlines that run edge to edge, answered by Instrument Serif italics that sound like the critic talking under his breath. Photos come first and fill their frames. The scroll is the narrator: sections pin, words light up, moons wax and numbers roll as you go. There is one visual world and no light/dark switch; sections alternate between night (ink) and paper, with royal blue bands reserved for the loudest moments.\n\nDensity is low and scale is extreme. Type sizes jump from 12px uppercase labels straight to 150–560px display words with little in between, which is what makes it feel like print rather than an app.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Night, moonlight and one family of blues; no theme switch.",
      "Variable-width grotesk: wide (112–125%) for names and headlines, condensed (62%) for numerals.",
      "Serif italic for every human aside: headlines of reviews, ledes, signatures.",
      "The moon phase is the score, the icon and the ornament.",
      "Flat surfaces, outlined and stamped controls, no shadows at rest.",
      "Motion is scroll-driven and always has a reduced-motion fallback."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Two Blues Rule",
        "body": "Royal blue (`--band`) is for surfaces with white type; sky glow (`--glow`) is light on the night. When something needs emphasis, make it blue, bigger or inverted, never a new hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paper Rule",
        "body": "On paper, blue text is `--glow-text` or `--band`, never `--glow`. Sky glow only sits on ink, petrol or the blue bands.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Token-Only Rule",
        "body": "Style with the CSS variables in `src/styles/global.css` (or their Tailwind aliases like `bg-glow`, `text-ink`). The only literals allowed are `#fff` over photos, black alpha gradients that keep text legible on images, and the off-screen colours above. A new colour goes into `global.css` (or the off-screen list) and this file's frontmatter together; `pnpm check:design` fails otherwise.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Width Axis Rule",
        "body": "Hierarchy comes from `font-stretch`, not new fonts: 125% display, 118% headline, 112% names, 88% manifesto, 62% numerals. Use `.wide` for 125%.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Optical Edge Rule",
        "body": "Display type is aligned by its ink, not its box. Left-aligned headings take the `.flush` class (pulls them 0.06em left so the letters sit on the gutter the labels use); centred ones cancel the trailing negative tracking with `padding-right` equal to it.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Italic Voice Rule",
        "body": "Anything that sounds like Alberto speaking (a quote, a lede, a sign-off) is Instrument Serif italic. Labels and data never are.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-At-Rest Rule",
        "body": "Cards, rows, stamps and buttons never carry a shadow. Hover is shown by inversion (paper → ink), scale on photos, or a small rotate, not by lifting.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do put a moon on every new surface, drawn with `moon.astro` and themed through its three variables.",
      "Do alternate scenes between ink, paper and (rarely) a royal-blue band, with 14vh/16vh section padding and a 24px gutter.",
      "Do use the width axis for hierarchy: 118–125% for headlines, 62% for numbers, tabular figures on any score.",
      "Do write quotes, ledes and sign-offs in Instrument Serif italic.",
      "Do use deep royal (#0b4d82) or royal blue (#115b96) for blue text and focus outlines on paper, and sky glow (#58b8ff) only on ink, petrol or the blue bands.",
      "Do drive motion with GSAP through `gsap.matchMedia()`, gating hidden start states behind the `.motion` class so reduced-motion visitors get the finished page."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add a hue outside the blues or a light/dark toggle; the site is one night.",
      "Don't add shadows to cards, rows, stamps or buttons at rest.",
      "Don't hardcode colours outside the tokens, except `#fff` and black alpha gradients over photos.",
      "Don't show scores as stars or plain numbers in a badge; a score is a moon phase and \"lunas\".",
      "Don't introduce another display or body font; stretch Archivo instead.",
      "Don't use `overflow-x: hidden` on page wrappers; use `clip` so sticky scenes keep working."
    ]
  }
}
